Usage of jobq:
jobq runs jobs from standard input, one per line: NAME MS [FLAKY] [fatal].
  -attempts int
    	how many times a job is tried (default 3)
  -backoff-ms ms
    	the wait in ms after a first failed try; it doubles after each (default 100)
  -burst int
    	how many jobs may start at once (default 2)
  -every-ms ms
    	the ms between starts after a burst; 0 for no limit (default 100)
  -live
    	run the jobs on real tasks on the host's clock
  -max-ms ms
    	the longest wait in ms between tries (default 1000)
  -workers int
    	how many jobs run at once (default 2)
